# The directory must exist for Yazi to find the flavor, but its content is
# generated: wallust renders flavor.toml in here on every wallpaper change
# (see wallust.toml [templates]; the source of truth is the
# templates/yazi-flavor.toml.j2 file in the repo). Until the very first
# render (apply-wallpaper.sh runs `wallust run` at every sway session start)
# Yazi starts with its built-in default colors.
*
!.gitignore
